WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:04.410
- Former President Trump, leaves office

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:06.850
with one last parting shot of corruption

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:09.040
because of course he would.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:12.470
His last acts in office
included a raft of pardons

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:14.080
that are bad.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:17.620
They are historically bad,
even without the prior pardons

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:20.989
and grants of clemency that
involve pardoning Paul Manafort

00:00:20.989 --> 00:00:22.670
and a bunch of his cronies,

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:24.670
this would have been
amongst the most corrupt

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:27.700
and despicable group
of pardons in history.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:29.500
But even as bad as they are,

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.280
it's hard not to take a step back

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:36.120
and recognize that it could
have been so, so much worse.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.160
But finally, it seems
that there might actually

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:39.510
be a silver lining here,

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:42.500
because the bar was so
low with this presidency

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.420
that we can finally step over it for once.

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:46.800
So, let's take stock and let's see

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.550
the good and the bad here.

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:50.710
Let's start with the bad news first.

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:55.210
Because these pardons are bad.
They are historically bad.

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:57.300
We start with a pardon for friend

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.450
of the president, Steve Bannon.

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:01.920
Bannon was facing a trial
for fraud in connection

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:03.740
to the "Build the Wall" campaign,

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:06.990
and all signs point to Bannon
stealing millions of dollars

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:09.560
from actual Trump supporters.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:12.470
And it's also notable that other
"Build The Wall" defendants

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:15.150
who have also been accused
and indicted of fraud

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:16.000
were not pardoned.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.290
It was just the president's friend.

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:20.217
As former representative.
Justin Amash said,

00:01:20.217 --> 00:01:21.910
"It went from Mexico will pay for it,

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:24.910
to you will pay for it to,
you will pay Steve Bannon,

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:27.240
and I will pardon him for defrauding you."

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:28.840
There's no good reason for this pardon.

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:31.120
There's no reason at all for this pardon

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:32.870
except that it's good to be a friend

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:35.310
of Donald Trump and swear omerta to him.

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:37.590
And that of course takes
us to another good friend

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:39.570
of Donald Trump, Elliot Broidy,

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:41.640
who pleaded guilty last year to conspiring

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:43.720
to violate foreign lobbying laws,

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:45.770
to influence the Trump administration

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:48.310
on behalf of Chinese
and Malaysian interests.

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:50.350
And he of course was implicated

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:54.260
in what is now known as
a pay for pardon scheme.

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:56.980
Is there anything corrupt
with this particular pardon

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:59.798
for a Republican fundraiser
who happens to be friend

00:01:59.798 --> 00:02:02.500
with the former president?

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:05.500
All signs point to yes on that one.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:08.190
And then there were more
pardons for corrupt Republicans,

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:10.580
like Rick Renzi and Duke Cunningham.

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:12.350
Renzi is a Republican and former member

00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:15.230
of the house who was sentenced
to three years in prison

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:17.140
in connection with a bribery scheme

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:18.920
related to real estate.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:22.100
Cunningham also pleaded
guilty to taking $2.4 million

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.513
in bribes from military contractors.

00:02:24.513 --> 00:02:26.910
These are not good people.

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:28.060
And there's just this pattern

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:31.870
of pardoning outright criminal corruption.

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:33.300
We'd never seen anything like it

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:34.980
with presidential pardons before.

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:37.160
Yes, a lot of former
presidents seem to have a habit

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:38.410
of pardoning light corruption

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:40.280
for those who happen to be well connected,

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:41.480
but here, the worse the corruption,

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:42.760
the more likely to get a pardon.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:46.190
And the corrupt are a
preponderance of the pardons.

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:48.190
It exists on both sides of the aisle.

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:49.640
While there's certainly a preponderance

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:51.950
of corrupt Republicans
who have received pardons,

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:54.920
that pattern continued with
pardoning former Detroit mayor,

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:57.590
Kwame Kilpatrick, who
was convicted in 2013

00:02:57.590 --> 00:02:59.830
for using his office to enrich himself

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:03.730
through kickbacks, shakedowns
and bid rigging schemes.

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:06.470
President Trump was clearly
favoring his friends

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:09.130
and business partners,
but at the same time,

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:10.680
he was just setting a precedent

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.960
for absolving pure corruption.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:16.050
Pure political and business
related corruption.

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:18.377
As political commentator,
Josh Barro put it,

00:03:18.377 --> 00:03:20.530
"They only make sense
as a general statement

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:22.450
that corruption is good."

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:24.270
And that pattern of pardoning

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.940
just outright corruption,

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:28.670
specifically with an emphasis
on real estate corruption,

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:31.910
continues with the list of
people who received pardons.

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:34.050
For example, Sholam
Weiss, who was sentenced

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:36.200
to more than 800 years in
prison for racketeering,

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:39.540
fraud and money laundering
related to insurance fraud.

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:41.960
And then Eliyahu Weinstein,
who was sentenced

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:43.220
to more than 20 years in prison

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:44.820
for a real estate Ponzi scheme

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:47.580
that cost $200 million in damages.

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:49.630
And then oddly, Anthony Levandowski,

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:52.410
who pleaded guilty to stealing IP related

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:55.590
to driverless cars when he
left Google to go to Uber.

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:58.560
And the list of overtly
corrupt individuals

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:01.270
who received a pardon is extremely long.

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:04.880
But lest you think that Trump
was only pardoning corruption,

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:06.840
he also engaged in pure cronyism.

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:09.560
Like pardoning New York
observer's Ken Kurson,

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:12.360
who was charged with
cyber-stalking last fall,

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:14.220
and who happens to be a very, very

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.960
good friend of Jared Kushner.

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:20.670
And then as potentially the
very last act in office,

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:23.840
president Trump had one
last pardon to dish out

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:27.680
after the raft that he released
at 1:30 in the morning.

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:29.370
He also pardoned Albert Pirro,

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:31.880
who was a real estate
developer and notably

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:36.200
was the ex-husband of judge
Jeanine Pirro from Fox news.

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:38.010
Pirro had been convicted of conspiracy

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:39.330
and tax evasion in 2000.

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:42.540
And they had actually
represented Trump himself

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:44.160
in some real estate deals.

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:47.190
To say that these people
are undeserving of pardons

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:50.260
is a vast, vast understatement.

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:52.300
And of course, potentially
as a cherry on top,

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:53.830
at one o'clock in the morning,

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:57.130
president Trump revoked his
2017 "Drain the Swamp" memo,

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.600
which prevented members of the White House

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:01.890
from lobbying the
government for five years

00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:04.540
so that the members of his administration

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:06.790
can now lobby the government.

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:11.790
- It is time to drain the
swamp in Washington, DC.

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:13.950
- In retrospect, looking
at all of these actions

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:16.330
which were entirely foreseeable,

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:18.330
it's not hard to see
why people who thought

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:21.110
that president Trump was the
anti-corruption president

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:23.340
and would actually drain the swamp,

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:25.860
also happened to believe in
stupid conspiracy theories

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:29.130
and absurd prognostications
that never came true.

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:30.740
But, if you did believe any of

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:33.850
those preposterously dumb
things, please contact me.

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:36.460
I have some really interesting
investment opportunities.

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:38.490
You might even call them unbelievable.

00:05:38.490 --> 00:05:41.660
But let's also take
stock that this actually

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:45.520
could have been much, much worse.

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:47.910
President Trump could
have pardoned himself

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:51.260
and caused an actual
constitutional crisis.

00:05:51.260 --> 00:05:53.220
Now, of course, the masochistic sportsman

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:54.900
in me kind of wanted to see it,

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:57.060
just so that that theory
that the president

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:59.540
could pardon himself would be smacked down

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:00.930
in front of the Supreme court

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:04.920
as part of a Trump corruption
and criminal investigation.

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:06.710
It's also entirely possible that Trump

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:09.420
could have pardoned members of
his family, including Ivanka,

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:10.810
Jared Kushner, Don Jr.

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:12.600
Eric, Kimberly Guilfoyle.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:15.100
And it appears that he really
really wanted to do that,

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:17.940
but then White House
counsel, Pat Cipollone,

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:19.560
said it would open Trump himself

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:23.140
up to personal liability
or criminal liability.

00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:26.680
And so the reason for him
not undertaking these actions

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:28.890
which he apparently wanted to do,

00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:31.700
is that Donald Trump
is selfish to the core

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:34.510
and is willing to throw his
own children under the bus.

00:06:34.510 --> 00:06:35.880
It's possible that he could have pardoned

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:38.270
his own personal attorney, Rudy Giuliani,

00:06:38.270 --> 00:06:41.450
who's under investigation for
many fraud related things.

00:06:41.450 --> 00:06:43.470
It's also entirely possible
that president Trump

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:45.770
could have pardoned his own
personal business associates.

00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:48.410
Like, Trump Organization
CFO, Allen Weisselberg,

00:06:48.410 --> 00:06:49.680
who also has been implicated

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:52.100
in all kinds of Trump related fraud.

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:54.240
He could have pardoned
the Capitol rioters.

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:56.700
He could have pardoned
some of the Congress people

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:59.870
who helped to foment some
of the Capitol riots,

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:02.830
including Congressmen Biggs and Gosar,

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:05.750
who apparently sought
pardons for their role

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:07.970
in creating the Capitol riots.

00:07:07.970 --> 00:07:10.600
And one has to ask, if you're looking

00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:11.980
for a preemptive pardon,

00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:15.320
are you worried about criminal
liability related there too?

00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:17.670
I'm going to cover this
in a video shortly.

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:19.660
We're lucky that there were only a handful

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:21.720
of celebrity pardons for some reason.

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:23.930
Including Lil Wayne, Kodak Black

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:25.740
and Harry-O of Death Row Records.

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:27.520
And Joe Exotic of Tiger King fame

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:29.260
is not amongst the pardonees.

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:32.220
And the ultimate good news
is that none of these pardons

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:34.040
affect the impeachment trial in the Senate

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:36.740
that remains in the short term horizon.

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:39.360
And of course, a new department of justice

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:41.900
can create new criminal investigations

00:07:41.900 --> 00:07:44.710
and unearth all of the untoward doings

00:07:44.710 --> 00:07:47.260
of the late Trump presidency.

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:49.540
Of course, it's going to
take a long, long time

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:52.440
to undo the damage of
the Trump presidency.

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:54.540
But, like allowed orange fart,

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:58.460
the noxious Trump presidency
is already departing the room.

00:07:58.460 --> 00:07:59.880
And of course it's important to recognize

00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:02.400
that none of this was normal.

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:04.660
The Trump presidency ended like it began

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:07.030
as former president George Bush said,

00:08:07.030 --> 00:08:08.800
with some weird (beep).

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:11.460
And I look forward to covering
the Biden administration.

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:13.810
I will cover any dubious legal strategies

00:08:13.810 --> 00:08:15.060
that they undertake.

00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:17.270
My lawsuit against the
White House will continue

00:08:17.270 --> 00:08:20.470
because it's about transparency
not about partisanship.

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:24.380
But make no mistake, the last
four years were not normal.

00:08:24.380 --> 00:08:27.430
And as a reminder, Donald
Trump is now a private citizen,

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:29.950
to the extent that he ever
had immunity as president,

00:08:29.950 --> 00:08:32.690
he no longer has immunity for anything.

00:08:32.690 --> 00:08:35.010
These pardons are largely unjust,

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:37.660
but they likely won't have
systemic reverberations.

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:41.150
Or at least those reverberations
should be dampened.

00:08:41.150 --> 00:08:45.130
Many who received these
pardons might even face civil

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:47.450
and state-based criminality down the line.

00:08:47.450 --> 00:08:49.110
These pardons are bad,

00:08:49.110 --> 00:08:51.970
but they're likely not earth shattering.

00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:53.648
By all appearances, the damage of

00:08:53.648 --> 00:08:58.648
the Trump administration was
extensive but it's contained.

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:01.533
And now it's time to clean up the mess.

